% text-order on every sort by a text or untyped key (SEL-0060).
%
% SEL sorts number-shaped text as numbers and other text by its bytes (the
% comparison every sort uses); SQL sorts a text key by its bytes throughout. A
% text column holding "10", "9" and "100" sorts 9, 10, 100 in SEL and
% 10, 100, 9 on MariaDB 11.8 (sql/oracle/statements.json witnesses it on every
% server). No ORDER BY can reproduce SEL's comparison for text that may or may
% not look numeric, so the difference is declared rather than hidden: text-order
% on the fragment, fatal under strict, so the planner sorts in memory there. A
% key that is a number -- a NUM column, arithmetic, a numeric CANON -- sorts
% as SEL sorts it and carries nothing.

### name: order.postgresql.text-key-is-translated
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> SORT_BY(_["t"])
--- expect
SELECT * FROM "r" ORDER BY CAST("t" AS TEXT) COLLATE "C" ASC
===

### name: order.postgresql.text-key-is-refused-under-strict
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> SORT_BY(_["t"])
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:15
===

### name: order.postgresql.num-key-is-exact
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> SORT_BY(_["n"])
--- expect
SELECT * FROM "r" ORDER BY "n" ASC
===

