### name: order.mariadb.untyped-key-is-refused-under-strict
--- note
An untyped column is whatever the server holds; text there sorts by its
bytes as a declared one does.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "U": {"kind": "column", "column": "u"}}}}
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> SORT_BY(_["u"])
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:15
===

### name: order.mariadb.computed-text-key-is-refused-under-strict
--- note
A computed text key is text all the same: "10" and "9" sort as numbers in
SEL whatever made them.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> SORT_BY(LEFT(_["t"], 5))
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:14
===

### name: order.mariadb.arithmetic-key-is-exact
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> SORT_BY(_["n"] + 2)
--- expect
SELECT * FROM `r` ORDER BY (`n` + 2) ASC
===

### name: order.mariadb.a-text-group-key-is-refused-under-strict
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> BUCKET(_["t"], RECORD("k", _K, "c", COUNT(_))) .> SORT_BY(_["k"])
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:65
===

### name: order.mariadb.a-numeric-group-key-is-exact
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> BUCKET(_["n"], RECORD("k", _K, "c", COUNT(_))) .> SORT_BY(_["k"])
--- expect
SELECT MIN(`n`) AS `k`, COUNT(*) AS `c` FROM `r` GROUP BY CAST(`n` AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin ORDER BY MIN(`n`) ASC
===

### name: plan.order.strict-sorts-text-in-memory.mariadb
--- note
Under strict the text sort is refused, and the planner keeps it in memory
over the rows the SQL filtered.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- source
R .> FILTER(_["n"] > 1) .> SORT_BY(_["t"])
--- plan
hybrid
--- tables
r
--- expect
SELECT * FROM `r` WHERE (`n` > 1)
===
